{% extends "../layout.njk" %}
{% block headStylesheets %}
<link rel="preload" as="style" href="/pages/hummey.css">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/pages/hummey.css">
{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<div class="hummey-banner">
    <img src="/assets/projects/hummey/Hummey_header.png" alt="Hummey Banner">
</div>
<div class="project">
    <div class="hummey-explainer">
        <img src="/assets/projects/hummey/Running_Loop_on_Jar_4x6.gif">
        <p>
            Hummey is a fictional honey brand created in
            collaboration with a designer, exploring a warm,
            playful and organic visual identity.
            </br></br>
            My role was to bring the brand to life through
            motion, taking the existing identity and developing
            a range of animated and interactive assets. Across
            hand—drawn animation, social content, interactive
            branding and product—focused motion, I explored how
            movement could add personality and depth to the
            brand.
            </br></br>
            The project allowed me to experiment with different
            approaches to motion while keeping a consistent
            visual language, from tactile frame—by—frame
            animation to interactive digital experiences and
            composited product visuals.
            </br></br>
            <b>Credits</b></br>
            <b>Brand Design:</b> Woo Designs</br>
            <b>Motion Design:</b> Alex Smith (Me!)</br>
        </p>
    </div>
    <img class="hummey-img" src="/assets/projects/hummey/Hummy_Logo_&_Bees.gif">
    <div class="hummey-text hummey-process">
        I explored a range of approaches to bring the Hummey identity beyond the static designs. I started with a
        hand—drawn, frame—by—frame cel animation of the logo, using the imperfections and tactile quality of the technique
        to reinforce the brand's natural, handcrafted character. I then developed three animated Instagram Stories, adapting
        the visual identity into short—form social content with a playful and engaging rhythm. To explore a more interactive
        direction, I created a responsive version of the logo in Rive, allowing the identity to react to user interaction 
        rather than simply playing as a fixed animation. Finally, I created a product—focused piece by compositing animation 
        directly onto a honey jar, combining the moving elements with Hummey's label and wider brand assets. Together, these 
        pieces allowed me to explore how motion could give the brand a more expressive and tangible presence across 
        different formats, from social content and interactive experiences to physical product.
    </div>
    <img src="/assets/projects/hummey/Insta_Story's_Combined.gif">
    <img src="/assets/projects/hummey/Have a play.svg" style="width: 15%; margin-bottom: -8%;">
    <canvas id="canvas-2" style="width: 100%; padding: 5% 10%;"></canvas>
    <div class="hummey-text">
        <h2>Toolkits & Rigs</h2></br></br>
        <h3>After Effects</h3></br></br>
        <p>
            For the character and logo animation, I used Duik Angela and Joysticks 'n Sliders to build
            flexible rigs and create expressive animation controls. These tools allowed me to work
            procedurally with the artwork, making it easier to experiment with movement and quickly iterate on
            I also allowed easier different animation states. </br></br>

            made use of Essential Graphics to build controls outside of the source compositions. This
            me to expose animation states and keyframes at a higher level, making the final animations
            to manage and adjust without needing to continually work inside the original compositions.
        </p>
    </div>
    <img class="hummey-triple-img" src="/assets/projects/hummey/Bee Rig BTS.gif">
    <img class="hummey-triple-img" src="/assets/projects/hummey/Bee Landing - Rig and Essential Graphics BTS.gif">
    <img class="hummey-triple-img" src="/assets/projects/hummey/Flower Running Rig BTS.gif">
    <div class="hummey-text">
        <h3>Rive</h3></br></br>
        <p>
            For the interactive logo, I used Rive's rigging and state—based animation tools to create a more
            responsive version of the Hummey identity. I used the bone system to animate the flower stem,
            while joysticks gave me control over the bee and different flower states. </br></br>

            I then used a ViewMode1 to connect these elements and create the interactive behaviour, allowing
            the different animation states to respond dynamically to user input. This gave the identity a more
            playful and reactive quality while keeping the animation system flexible and easy to control.
        </p>
    </div>
    <img class="hummey-double-left" src="/assets/projects/hummey/Rive_-_Flower_Rig_BTS.gif">
    <img class="hummey-double-right" src="/assets/projects/hummey/Rive_-_Interactive_logo_-_Viewmodel_Highlight.gif">
</div>
{% endblock %}
{% set riveInstances = [ "hummey" ] %}
